;; spec:   §4 (types §6.4, §8.4, §6.12 exception 5)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 2
;; audit:  clean
;; A protocol method passed as a function value. It type-checks
;; (count : (fn :send ((Vec i64)) i64) at this instantiation), and the
;; spec gives it a calling convention:
;;   types §8.4: "Named functions used as values are IMMORTAL closures
;;   whose code is the function's all-owned body ... The monomorphiser
;;   ... emits an all-owned body for every function whose value is taken
;;   anywhere in it ...; a protocol method's implementation used as a
;;   value likewise."
;;   types §6.12 exception 5: "through a function value every object
;;   parameter and the closure are owned, and a named function reached
;;   that way runs its all-owned body".
;;
;; Observed (fibref run):
;;   failed:
;;   004-method-as-function-value.fib:29:21: gap in the ownership plan: method
;;   count used as a function value: the plan has no all-owned body for a
;;   method (§8.4)
;; (map count [[1] [2 3]]) fails the same way inside the prelude's map,
;; and so do the arithmetic and deref methods: (apply2 + 1 2) gives "gap
;; in the ownership plan: method + used as a function value", and
;; (apply1 deref c) "method deref used as a function value".
;; Diagnosis: own (no all-owned body is planned for a method
;; implementation) and eval (which needs one); a builtin (str-len) or a
;; defun (box) as a value works.
(defun apply1 (f x) (f x))
(defun main () -> i64 (apply1 count (conj [5] 6)))
